# Overlay flair (example)

This file is an *example* of the personal/private instruction "flair" your
Overlay can carry. It is NOT loaded by the Base — copy it into your private
overlay repo and adapt it. Keep the public Base's `CLAUDE.md` neutral; put
personal preferences here.

Guidance (keep it lean — every line loads on every request; ~150–200 instruction
budget per the master research):

- State your default engine and permission posture preferences here, not in the
  Base. Example: "Default engine: claude; posture: full-auto on this host."
- Reference your private skills/commands added via `substrateos_overlay.py`.
- Never put secrets here; use the gitignored `.env` of your overlay repo.
- Remember the one-way rule: this overlay depends on the Base, never the reverse.
